Intel HEX fixture for the end-to-end CLI test.
readHexFile skips any line not starting with ':', so this header is ignored.

Loads 10 bytes at $0200 exercising W65C02-only instructions:

  0200  0f 12 05   bbr0 $12, $0208   3-byte zp,rel -- the length bug
  0203  07 10      rmb0 $10
  0205  1a         inc a             accumulator mode
  0206  80 05      bra $020d
  0208  b2 10      lda ($10)         zero page indirect

On plain 65c02 the same bytes decode differently ($0f and $07 are NOPs
there), so this also proves --cpu is wired up.

:0A0200000F120507101A8005B21056
:00000001FF
